{
 "comment": "clause44: the four columns and the closed reasons. A supplier's GSTIN from its ledger, and from the voucher's own PARTYGSTIN (padded and lower case, which the reference strips and upper-cases) on a cash purchase and on a purchase from a ledger with none; composition from the client's map (padded, mixed case, a no-break space; 'Regular' is not composition; a composition ledger with no GSTIN stays unregistered); a voucher with input tax is 'other than composition', one without (or with a nil tax line) is 'exempt or non-GST'; a debit note's credit lines reduce the column; a nil expense line is no line; round-off rides with a voucher's real line and, alone or beside only salary, has no supplier; salary (configured as no supplier), depreciation, a journal with no party and one whose party is an income ledger; a party named on no ledger master; and a round-off line beside a real line on a journal with no party, which reads 'no party' like its sibling; round-off beside only a depreciation line, which takes that line's reason; round-off beside a real line on a voucher whose party is an income ledger, which reads 'party is a P&L ledger' like its sibling; and a PARTYGSTIN of 'URP', which the reference reads as a GSTIN like any non-blank text. Every GSTIN is invented (fourteenth character Y).",
